// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// queries.kql
// Project 5: Monitoring and Alerting Dashboard
// KQL (Kusto Query Language) queries against the AzureActivity table,
// populated by the subscription Activity Log diagnostic setting.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Query 1: Most recent subscription activity, newest first.
// project picks just the columns that matter - AzureActivity has dozens of
// columns by default, most irrelevant for a quick look at "what happened."
AzureActivity
| project TimeGenerated, OperationNameValue, ResourceGroup, Caller, ActivityStatusValue
| order by TimeGenerated desc
| take 50

// Query 2: Which resource group generated the most activity.
// A genuinely useful pattern - summarize + count groups rows and counts
// them, rather than you manually scrolling through hundreds of log lines.
AzureActivity
| summarize OperationCount = count() by ResourceGroup
| order by OperationCount desc

// Query 3: Failed operations only - the query that actually matters for
// monitoring, rather than just "what happened."
AzureActivity
| where ActivityStatusValue == "Failed"
| project TimeGenerated, OperationNameValue, ResourceGroup, Caller, ActivityStatusValue
| order by TimeGenerated desc
